[x] 3. Send your editor time to pairtime as well as to your WakaTime server

    WakaTime's editor plugins run wakatime-cli, which sends a heartbeat each
    time you edit or move around in a file to the server in your
    ~/.wakatime.cfg, such as Hackatime. pairtime adds one line under
    [api_urls] there, so that wakatime-cli also sends every heartbeat to
    pairtime's agent on this computer. Nothing else in the file changes.
    While pairtime's agent doesn't take what wakatime-cli sends it, as while
    the agent isn't running, wakatime-cli holds back what it sends your
    server too, and sends it once the agent takes it again.
    Your editors' own environment can hold a proxy that install can't see,
    and wakatime-cli would then send pairtime's copy of each heartbeat
    through it: the proxy would get your project and file names unencrypted,
    pairtime would get none of them, and each send the proxy doesn't pass on
    would hold back what wakatime-cli sends your own server. So don't set a
    proxy for your editors while pairtime's line is in.

    Saying no doesn't stop you from using pairtime.
    Without it, pairtime doesn't see the time you spend in an editor.
    You can take the line out any time with pairtime uninstall, which leaves
    the rest of the file as it was.

    --- /home/teen/.wakatime.cfg
    +++ /home/teen/.wakatime.cfg
    @@ -2,3 +2,6 @@
     api_url = ***
     api_key = ***
     heartbeat_rate_limit_seconds = ***
    +
    +[api_urls]
    +.+ = http://127.0.0.1:7247/api/v1|00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a9e7
